    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 294\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 7867-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the insurance law, in relation to Medicare part D\n      employer group waiver plans\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would amend the Insurance Law  to  exempt  insurers,  corpo-\nrations,  health  maintenance  organizations  or  municipal  cooperative\nhealth benefit plans who offer Medicare Part D group waiver  plans  from\ncomplying  with  rate  approval  and  filing  requirements issued by the\nDepartment of Financial Services (DFS).\n\n  This bill would significantly erode protections  for  New  York  State\nretirees. Insurers offering such coverage would no longer have to submit\ntheir policies and contracts for DFS approval. Removing DFS's regulatory\nand  enforcement  oversight would, in effect, de-regulate this insurance\nproduct. In addition, this bill applies retroactively back to January 1,\n2014, thereby making any conduct that was illegal  under  the  Insurance\nLaw  now  legal,  and  exempting issuers that violated the Insurance Law\nfrom any kind  of  penalty  or  discipline.  For  these  reasons,  I  am\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 294,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
